                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          #ProjectivelyCofibrantDiagram.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A functor/diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %strong projectively cofibrant diagram
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              if it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure"} projective model structure
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{D}, \mathcal{C}]_{proj}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              We unwind the condition in def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectivelyCofibrantDiagram"}
            %p
              First of all it says of course that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \colon \mathcal{D}\to \mathcal{C}
              is projectively cofibrant precisely if the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \to X
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
              diagram has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
              with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              of diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (A \stackrel{p}{\to} B) : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
            %p
              which are projective acyclic fibrations, hence which are such that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
              the component
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_c : A(c) \to B(c)
              is an acyclic fibration in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %p
              This in turn means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is projectively cofibrant precisely if for every diagram of natural transformations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp;A
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    \&amp;\downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    X
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    B
                    }
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              as above, there exists a lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi σ
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp;A
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{\sigma}}\nearrow &amp;\downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    X
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    B
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\in [\mathcal{D}, \mathcal{C}]
                    \\,.
            %p making the triangle commute.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            The main point of projectively cofibrant diagrams is that the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            over them is a presentation of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
          %p
            because the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊣
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
            constant diagram)-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi const
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi const
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim} \dashv const)
                  \:
                  \\mathcal{C} \stackrel{\overset{\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{const}{\to}}
                  [\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{D}]
          %p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            (because
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi const
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const
            is by the very definition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure"} projective model structure
            a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functor"} right Quillen functor
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕃
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟶
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{L}\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q X
            of a diagram
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕃
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathbb{L} \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim})(X)
                  \\simeq
                  \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim})(Q X)
                  \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#for_specific_diagram_shapes For specific diagram shapes
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
              diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \leftarrow X_0 \to X_2
              is projectively cofibrant precisely if the two morphisms are cofibrations in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            %p
              The colimit over such a diagram is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
              of the span.
          #CofibrantCotowerDiagram.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              A
              %em cotower
              diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_0 \to X_1 \to X_2 \to \cdots
            %p
              is projectively cofibrant precisely if every morphism is a cofibration and if the first object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            %p
              The colimit over such a diagram is a homotopy
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+colimit"} sequential colimit
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+morphisms"} parallel morphisms
              diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_0 \stackrel{\overset{f}{\to}}{\underset{g}{\to}} X_1
            %p
              is projectively cofibrant precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
              is cofibrant, and if the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,g) : X_0 \coprod X_0 \to X_1
              is a cofibration.
            %p
              This implies that also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              are cofibrations and hence that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              is cofibrant.
          %p
            The colimit over such a diagram is a homotopy
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
          %h3#for_specific_ambient_model_categories For specific ambient model categories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_{Quillen}
            be the standard
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi proj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{D}, \mathcal{C}]_{proj}
            is the projective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %p
            For the following see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            the section
            %em
              %a{:href => "model+structure%20on%20simplicial%20presheaves#CofibrantObjects"} Cofibrant objects
            for more details (due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Dugger"} Dan Dugger
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/questions/97690/necessary-conditions-for-cofibrancy-in-global-projective-model-structure-on-simp/127187#127187"} Richard Garner’s answer on MathOverflow
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A necessary and sufficient condition for a diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : \mathcal{D} \to sSet
              to be projectively cofibrant is:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is degreewise a coproduct of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mi i
                        %msubsup
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                          %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msubsup
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                          %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo ↪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X_n = \coprod_{i} U^n_i \;\;\;\;  \{U^n_i \in \mathcal{C} \hookrightarrow [\mathcal{C}, Set]\}
              %li
                %p
                  Each simplicial level, as a presheaf of sets, can be presented as the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  of two presheaves of sets, one of which is the presheaf of degenerate simplices:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi NonDegenerate
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %msub
                          %mi Degenerate
                          %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X_n = NonDegenerate_n \coprod Degenerate_n
                        \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+hypercover"} split hypercover
              is of this form.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : \mathcal{D} \to sSet
              any simplicial presheaf, a cofibrant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
              is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (Q X)_n : \coprod_{U_0 \to \cdots \to U_n \to X_n} U_0
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the coproduct runs over all sequences of morphisms between representables
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
          %h2#references References
          %p
            See the references at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
            and generally at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
          %p Related discussion is at
          %ul
            %li
              MathOverflow
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/70612/when-are-diagrams-of-cofibrations-projectively-cofibrant"} When are “diagrams of cofibrations” projectively cofibrant
          %p Related discussion is for instance also in
          %ul
            %li
              Urs Schreiber,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p where cofibrant cotowers are mentioned as example 2.3.15.
